# Syntax cheat sheet

The tags you will use most. Every example here is drawn live by Keydown!


::divider{poolside|Syntax cheat sheet|cyan}
## Lines

Start a line with one of these and a space:

| Write | You get |
| --- | --- |
| `# Heading` ... `###### Heading` | Heading levels 1 to 6 |
| `#= Heading` | The extra large #/C)mega header) |
| `* item` | A bullet point |
| `> text` | A quote |
| `-# text` | ++C2}Subtext++: small, dim text for notes |
| `::pagebreak` | A new page |

-# This line is subtext, drawn by `-# text`!

## Inline

| Write | You get |
| --- | --- |
| `**bold**` | ++R%]bold++ |
| `*italic*` | *italic* |
| Backticks around a word | `code` |
| `[link](https://radii-office.com)` | [link](https://radii-office.com) |
| Code with a style word after it | `Ctrl+K`{key} and `ls -la`{terminal} |

## Chips and highlights

Keydown's signature looks are made by wrapping words in a color code between symbols. The letters pick the color: R red, O orange, GL gold, Y yellow, L lime, G green, TU turquoise, T teal, C cyan, B blue, PR purple, PK pink.

| Write | You get |
| --- | --- |
| `++R+Aero chip++` | ++R+Aero chip++ |
| `#G#gel chip#` | #G#gel chip# |
| `!!#C#rim chip#` | !!#C#rim chip# |
| `%B%gloss pill%` | %B%gloss pill% |
| `=B=orb=B=` | =B=orb=B= |
| `#Y#highlight##` | #Y#highlight## |
| `^^B^speech bubble^^` | ^^B^speech bubble^^ |

Each of these has dozens or hundreds of cousins. See [Chips and styles](#/keydown-reference) for every one!

## Writing a symbol as itself

If you want to show a tag instead of using it, put a backslash before the symbols, like `\#R\#not a chip\#`. Words that only look like Keydown, such as AT&T and R&D, stay as typed!

## Math

`$E = mc^2$` gives $E = mc^2$, and a line with `$$ ... $$` gives a larger centered equation!

## Callouts

```
::note Your own title
Text inside the box.
::end
```

::note Your own title
Text inside the box. There are also tip, info, warning, danger, success and important!
::end

